    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a14">

                <pb facs="0368" n="1102" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1102"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 13 in No. 151.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rawicz to Mr. Peirce.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your two letters of the 5th instant
                    received to-day.</p>
                <p>In answer to the one concerning the telegram in re Yablkowski, dated 5th instant,
                    I have to inform you that comparing it with your letter it appears that a
                    mistake was made in the telegraphic office, where word “viséed” was given to me
                    in the dispatch as “used,” and that was the reason why my telegraphic answer was
                    not correct.</p>
                <p>I am awaiting the answer from the judge of Nieszawa to the telegram mentioned in
                    my yesterday’s letter, and after receipt I shall report to you immediately.</p>
                <p>In re Samuel Cinger I have no further communications from our consul at
                    Odessa.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph Rawicz</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
